WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:08.070
Programs need memory. Variables are how they remember scores, names, totals — anything that changes.

2
00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:11.120
A variable is a named storage location.

3
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.140
Set gives it a value; change adds to it.

4
00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.970
Its value can change while the program runs.

5
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.410
Ask and wait lets the user type.

6
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.040
Whatever they type is stored in answer.

7
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.310
Copy it into your own variable if you need it later.

8
00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:29.650
Arithmetic operators (+ − × ÷ mod) calculate.

9
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:34.110
Join sticks text together to build messages.

10
00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:41.370
Name variables for what they hold: score, lives, total — not x1 or thing.

11
00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:43.950
Clear names make code readable.

12
00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:50.300
In Python, input is like ask and wait, and the variables a and b store the numbers.

13
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.130
Great work! Let’s remember what we learned.

14
00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:57.280
Now build along, then try the challenges. You’ve got this!
